# Debian-provided pieces (the Sysible packages are included via config/packages.chroot)
gnome-core
gdm3
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
# Guest integration for VMware/VirtualBox/KVM (clipboard, auto-resize, folder
# sharing) — Sysible Workstation commonly runs in a VM, incl. Fusion on Apple Silicon.
open-vm-tools
open-vm-tools-desktop
# Right-click "Open in SysTerm": Nautilus python extension. The GNOME desktop-
# icons (DING) and dash-to-dock extensions are installed best-effort by the
# system hook (their Debian package names vary), so a missing one never aborts
# the ISO build.
python3-nautilus
firefox-esr
gnome-text-editor
# net-tools is already pulled via the metapackage; listed here explicitly so
# ifconfig is guaranteed present (its PATH is fixed via /etc/profile.d).
net-tools
# Graphical boot/shutdown splash — themed as Sysible (the system hook sets our
# theme as default and rebuilds the initramfs), replacing Debian's Plymouth theme.
plymouth
plymouth-themes
# glib-compile-resources — used by the system hook to rebuild the GNOME Shell
# theme gresource with the Sysible lock/login background.
libglib2.0-dev-bin
# SysTerm runtime deps (it's a GTK3/VTE terminal). The SysTerm .deb is built and
# included by build.sh, but gnome-core doesn't pull the VTE typelib — without
# these its dependency is unmet, so it fails to install/run and "Open Terminal"
# does nothing. Install them explicitly so SysTerm is present and launches.
python3-gi
gir1.2-gtk-3.0
gir1.2-vte-2.91
# Fallback terminal backstop. Every "Open Terminal" on Sysible routes through
# the sysible-term shim to SysTerm; if a bad SysTerm update ever fails to launch,
# the shim falls back to xterm so the user is never locked out of all terminals.
# Tiny, dependency-light, and guaranteed present for exactly this reason.
xterm
